      "review": "Eyes Wide Shut made me think, and it’ll take much more than just its runtime to dissect every little thing Kubrick meant to convey. I really appreciated Tom Cruise’s performance, its the best I’ve seen from him (likely because I’ve otherwise only ever seen him in the Mission: Impossible movies). I’d love to rewatch this movie, it seems like something that would reveal a lot more on a second viewing."
    },
    {
      "title": "The Odyssey",
      "year": "2026",
      "rating": 5.0,
      "watched": "2026-07-20",
      "rewatch": false,
      "url": "https://letterboxd.com/girff/film/the-odyssey-2026/",
      "poster": "https://a.ltrbxd.com/resized/film-poster/1/2/5/5/3/9/4/1255394-the-odyssey-2026-0-600-0-900-crop.jpg?v=1eed046d0c",
      "review": "The Odyssey is 2 hours and 53 minutes of pure filmmaking genius on display by one of the greatest directors still active today. It's a film so impactful that very little can encompass all that it is, but I can try.This film encompasses all that makes Christopher Nolan's filmography so great. The scale hits as hard as Inception, the performances resonate with me to the level of those in Oppenheimer, and the raw emotions I felt are equal to those in Interstellar.In regards to the scale, the use of music contributes just as much as anything with the camera. Ludwig Göransson's score doesn't leave…"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sleepy Hollow",
