    {
      "title": "Obsession",
      "year": "2025",
      "rating": 4.5,
      "watched": "2026-07-15",
      "rewatch": false,
      "url": "https://letterboxd.com/girff/film/obsession-2025/",
      "poster": "https://a.ltrbxd.com/resized/film-poster/1/2/3/4/4/7/2/1234472-obsession-2025-2-0-600-0-900-crop.jpg?v=cff6fc00b6",
      "review": "I know I’m a little late to the party but let me say, I’m so glad I finally watched this movie. Obsession is one of the few movies that I’d say I have absolutely no notes on, in the sense of how it is written. The script was extremely tight, every plot thread was executed so well it truly is an impressive feat. I came out the movie extremely unsettled, but also equally as impressed. Inde Navarrette’s performance deserves just as much praise. She manages to be so expressive and clearly demonstrate the magic of the One Wish Willow purely with her mannerisms."
    },
    {
      "title": "Swapped",
      "year": "2026",
      "rating": 4.0,
      "watched": "2026-07-14",
      "rewatch": false,
      "url": "https://letterboxd.com/girff/film/swapped-2026/",
      "poster": "https://a.ltrbxd.com/resized/film-poster/9/0/7/8/6/8/907868-swapped-2026-0-600-0-900-crop.jpg?v=c7bb59e165",
      "review": "It’s been a while since I’ve watched a movie that was clearly aimed towards kids, so I expected your average modern Disney movie (i.e. a not very good movie). However, I was pleasantly surprised with the amount of real lessons and heart that was put into Swapped. At its core the movie is about learning what it’s like to be in someone else’s shoes, quite literally, and that message is taught alongside a story that isn’t without its plot twists. A full package of a beautiful art style and good voice acting performances pushes this movie to really be enjoyable."
    },
